==English==
{{wikipedia|lang=en}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|iːvəl|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
From Middle English {{term|wevel|lang=enm}}, from Old English {{term|wifel|lang=ang}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*wibilaz}} (compare Dutch tort{{term|tortwevel|wevel|dung beetle|lang=nl}}, Low German Scharn''wevel'', German {{term|Wiebel||beetle, chafer|lang=de}}), from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*webʰel}} (compare Lithuanian {{term|vãbalas||beetle, weevil|lang=lt}}, dialectal Russian {{term|ве́блица||intestinal worm|lang=ru}}), from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*webʰ-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*h₁webʰ-||to weave, wave}}. More at {{l|en|weave}} and {{l|en|wave}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any of several small [[herbivorous]] [[beetle|beetles]] in the superfamily [[Curculionoidea]]. Many of them have a distinctive snout.
# Any of several small herbivorous beetles in the family [[Curculionidae]] belonging to the superfamily ''Curculionoidea''.
# Any of several similar but more distantly related beetles such as the [[biscuit weevil]].

====Synonyms====
